WIN PREMIUM STAKES v1.0.0 — FROZEN DEFINITIONS

Question
How large is foregoing the win in familiar rating units? These are descriptive
scales. They neither identify subjective utility nor show a causal effect of
stakes on generosity. Never divide the premium by the rating level: a rating's
zero is arbitrary.

Sample
Use the frozen pool, observed nonadjacent 24-month main panel, November 2023 to
October 2025. Apply exact author exclusion (__PRIVATE_VALUE_1__ and __PRIVATE_VALUE_2__, either player).
Primary opportunities have engine_eval_cp_disconnected >= -100. Supported speeds
are ultrabullet, bullet, blitz, rapid and classical. Retain all other main-panel
selection rules; add no ply or rating-gap screen. Correspondence and other speeds
are outside this report and counted in sample_coverage.csv. Reports distinguish
all competitive opportunities, grants, chooser RD <= 110, and their intersection.
RD <= 110 is a rating-uncertainty restriction, not a tenure definition.

Premium and percentile cost
Draw post-rating = pre-rating + chooser_draw_payoff_v2.
Win post-rating  = pre-rating + chooser_win_payoff_v2.
Premium = win post-rating - draw post-rating. Verify against the certified premium.
The fields are model-based counterfactual rating updates, not rounded PGN updates.

For each speed and preceding calendar month, construct an empirical CDF from one
rating observation per account active in that month's existing chronology: its
latest pregame rating. Exclude the two author accounts. Keep other players'
factual rating histories, including games against those accounts. A missing
latest rating or conflicting ratings at tied latest starts excludes that account
from that snapshot and is reported. No RD filter is available for this population.
This is an observed-history reference population, not the live Lichess leaderboard
or a claim of complete platform coverage. Historical chronology and main-panel
coverage can differ; every focal game must still reconcile exactly on IDs, colors,
ratings and start times (API/PGN tolerance 1000ms).

F(r) = fraction of those accounts with rating <= r, including ties.
Cost in percentile points = 100 [F(win post-rating) - F(draw post-rating)].
Both alternatives use exactly the same lagged reference population. Standings
use 100 F(pre-rating). Compute row-specific costs, THEN medians/quantiles; do not
apply the median premium to a nonlinear CDF and call it the median cost. Deciles
are speed/month-relative; rating bands also have speed-specific tables.

Personal variation
For each focal opportunity, take the preceding 100 same-speed pregame rating
observations in strictly earlier recorded starts; exclude every equal-time start.
Align the API anchor to the focal game's own chronology second before looking
back, so it cannot count itself. Use sample SD (denominator 99). Repeat with 50
observations, the 100-observation IQR, and residual SD after a linear trend in
game sequence (denominator 98). The trend diagnostic is not a claim that trends
are known in real time beyond these past observations.

Primary ratio = premium / prior SD100. Also show premium / SD50, IQR100 and
detrended SD100. All observations in a window must have finite positive ratings. If a tie
in recorded starts straddles the last-100 or last-50 cutoff, that window is
unavailable. Missing, insufficient and zero-variation windows remain explicit
coverage categories. Zero or numerical-zero denominators (<= 1e-9) give missing
ratios, never infinity. Do not hide these players when interpreting coverage.
Report the calendar span of the 100 observations and time since the last one.
A short-lived run of stable ratings and a long dormant history are different.

Default history begins August 2023 (three preceding months before the study).
For any row with 100 observed strictly earlier starts, that last-100 window is
complete within the authenticated monthly source sequence. Earlier unknown starts
cannot change those 100 most recent observations. Other rows remain unavailable;
there is no claim of lifetime coverage. --history-start permits an earlier warm-up
and creates a separate cache. Never silently substitute a smaller window.

Ordinary-win units
Not estimated from this source. Its utc_ms field is a start timestamp. A realized
rating difference/outcome from an earlier-started game may still have been unknown
at the focal start. A future extension should authenticate completion timestamps,
select strictly completed prior same-speed games, identify ordinary wins from
verified scores/status, require enough wins, and show the number/span used.
No result_code encoding is guessed and no start is relabeled as completion.

Thresholds and weighting
Report whether the win post-rating crosses a 100-point boundary while the draw
does not, and analogous crossings of selected historical percentiles. These are
descriptive contrasts, not a threshold-effect regression. No lifetime personal
best is claimed. Main summaries weight opportunities equally. The equal-account
sensitivity first takes medians within account and speed, then medians across
accounts within speed. Account is a username identity, not necessarily a person.
The same-sample sensitivity compares all four variation denominators on their
intersection of valid observations. Quantile bands are distributional spread,
not confidence intervals. No standard errors or significance claims are made.

Validation and storage
Frozen main SHA256 checks; source history row/byte/schema checks; run-bound raw
Parquet footer digests and filesystem fingerprints; exact focal reconciliation;
duplicate and count-conservation gates; numerical unit tests and multi-month
synthetic pipeline tests. The historical manifest's legacy footer signature has
an undocumented serialization. This runner does not pretend its raw-footer digest
reproduces that signature or authenticates every source byte. Source history is
read-only. PRIVATE local work contains account/game rows. Only aggregate reports
are bundled. No API requests, rating replay or Stockfish execution.
